# System
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Root hygiene: allowlist top-level entries; anything else at root is ignored ──
# WHY: tools (screenshot CLIs, brain-explain, youtube-digest, playwright-mcp, …) write to
# their CWD, which is usually a checkout. `/*` makes EVERY new root file/dir ignored by
# default, so stray tool output never clutters `git status` or risks a commit. The
# specific denylist rules further down still refine WITHIN these re-included directories.
# Add a new legit framework top-level entry → add a matching `!/name` line here.
/*
!/.claude/
!/.cursorrules
!/.githooks/
!/.github/
!/.gitignore
!/.windsurfrules
!/CHANGELOG.md
!/CLAUDE.md
!/docs/
!/LICENSE
!/NOTICE
!/README.md
!/scripts/
!/SECURITY.md
!/setup.sh
!/system/
!/templates/
!/VERSION

# Environment
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Logs
*.log

# Node
node_modules/

# Local analysis caches
.pi-lens/

# Machine-generated Pi extension tsconfig (generated by bootstrap-pi-macos.sh)
system/pi-config/extensions/tsconfig.json

# Obsidian (tracked minimal config; ignore machine/user state)
.obsidian/cache/
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/graph.json

# Obsidian community plugins (often contain user-specific state or tokens)
.obsidian/plugins/
.obsidian/community-plugins.json
.obsidian/hotkeys.json

# Brain runtime config (generated by setup.sh; machine-specific)
brain.json

# Factory layout: where THIS machine's checkouts live. Same class as
# brain.json — shipping it would hand every user one machine's directory
# structure. Absent is a valid state: brain.sh falls back to the side-by-side
# suffix convention, which is what a normal install has.
factory.json

# Personal layer (never committed). `vault` is the symlink setup creates from the
# checkout to the vault outside it (~/.agentBrain/vault by default); the anchored bare
# form ignores the link itself so `git add -A` can never sweep the machine-specific
# link in. `local` is the retired name of that same link (CHANGELOG v1.10.2): setup
# no longer creates it, but an older install may still carry it, so it stays ignored
# as a directory (trailing slash) and as a symlink (bare form).
/vault
/local/
/local

# Shared knowledge layer — its own git repo, never swept into framework git
# (mirrors the vault/ handling above; the anchored form also ignores a `shared` SYMLINK)
shared/
/shared

# Temporary Pi files and session data
.pi/agent/auth.json
.pi/agent/sessions/

# Personal/private agentBrain layers that must never be shared
learnings/*-Memories/
system/Security/

# brain-hide-forget: forget batches and the runtime caches. They live in the vault,
# so the /vault rule above already covers them (and /local on an older install);
# listed here for clarity.
vault/.trash/**
vault/.hidden-index.json
vault/.parks-index.json
local/.trash/**
local/.hidden-index.json
local/.parks-index.json

# Local (non-shared) markdown — convention for personal/project context
*.local.md

# Graphify outputs — generated by `brain-graph build`, which writes to the workspace
# derived/ lane (~/.agentBrain/workspace/derived/graphify, see scripts/lib/workspace.sh),
# outside the checkout. Belt-and-braces guard against any in-tree graphify-out/ dirs
# that appear if a build is interrupted before its move.
graphify-out/
# Older installs linked system/graphify-out to the vault's graphify output. Nothing
# creates that link any more; a leftover one is a symlink, not a directory, so the
# trailing-slash pattern above does not catch it and this line does.
system/graphify-out

# Rust build artifacts (scanman rust-impl)
rust-impl/target/

# Runtime/tool output that can land in the checkout root when a tool is pointed
# at AGENTBRAIN_DIR instead of the live vault (screenshot tool output, stray addon
# data dirs, playwright-mcp page dumps). These are never part of the public
# framework; ignoring them keeps the working tree and `git add -A` clean.
/vault/
.playwright-mcp/
# Loose screenshots dropped in the checkout root (macOS screencapture, ad-hoc UI
# grabs, playwright/manual captures). Root-anchored (leading /) so images tracked
# deeper in the tree (docs, skill assets) still ship.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
.superpowers/

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Obsidian machine state never ships as a seed
templates/vault/.obsidian/workspace*.json
templates/vault/.obsidian/graph.json

# Addons that must never be published. The directory is the decision: private is
# the default, and moving an addon into system/addons/ is the deliberate act
# that makes it public. Fails closed, unlike a manifest field where forgetting
# it grants permission. check-addon-distribution.sh verifies this rule still
# holds, including the dangerous middle state where a file here is tracked
# anyway: release.sh builds from git ls-files, so a tracked file ships whatever
# this line says.
/system/addons-private/
